# REGRESSION (`todo/t0841`, R48 Track D1) — the DICT arm of the same class.
#
# `Expr::DictComprehension` is one of the three comprehension arms that walked
# their body in a single pass instead of the loop back-edge two-pass dance
# (`src/ir/lowering/liveness.rs`). The loop-invariant owned name `s` sits in
# the VALUE position here, so the dict's own free runs the string destructor
# once per stored alias.
#
# AXIS CELL: comprehension kind = DICT · body sub-position = VALUE ·
# source = RANGE · value type = String (heap-forced), key type = int.
# The int key is deliberate: a HEAP key would additionally trip `todo/t0121`
# (the dedup-discard leak), which is a different class and would make this cell
# unable to sit in the ASan sweep.
#
# RED-VERIFIED at pre-fix HEAD, both lanes: run rc 134, `free(): double free
# detected in tcache 2` (C and `--backend=llvm`); `--sanitize` reports
# `AddressSanitizer: attempting double-free`.

from std.collections import Dict

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    String s = mk("a", "b")
    Dict[int, String] d = {i: s for i in 0..3}
    print(d.len())
    print(d[0])
    print(d[2])
